     "result_text_tail": "arnings remain and don't affect the content:\n  - Two figures are written as words in the pack (\"four months\", \"four years\"), so the check can't match them.\n  - The market-growth branch can't be influenced by Onsoo, but it is kept because it decides whether to enter at all.\n\n**Choices I made in your absence**\n- **Format:** a deep deck with an issue tree, because this is a board decision.\n- **Look:** the navy theme.\n- **$40M ambition:** I read \"on the way to $40M by 2030\" as a direction, not a hard test. The slide's footnote asks the board to confirm.\n- **Awareness base:** Onsoo's 4% is among all survey respondents, which is the same base the retail sell-through table uses.\n- **Out of scope:** routes the planning team didn't model (mass retail, brand-website-led, distributor, acquisition) and launching in the US and Japan in the same year.\n- **Tariff:** the 25% duty is applied from 2027, before the mid-2027 ruling, so those cases are conservative.\n- **Japan's cash:** the pack has no inventory data for Japan, so its cash equals its operating result. This flatters Japan slightly.\n- **Next step 1:** the board gets the case back if US cash need passes $3.9M, the full-volume cost-stress peak. That threshold is my proposal.\n\nPossible next steps: switch theme, cut it to a 15\u201320 slide board version, or add a scenario (for example, retail added only once awareness passes 20%).\n\nFiles are in `./deliverable/`:\n- `onsoo-us-entry.pptx`\n- `onsoo-us-entry-sources.xlsx`\n- `onsoo-us-entry.json`"
    }
